<h1>Recon-Pipeline</h1>

<h2>Automated Reconnaissance & Attack Surface Discovery</h2>

<p>
  Recon-Pipeline is a cybersecurity automation project designed
  to streamline reconnaissance activities during authorised
  security assessments and bug bounty investigations.
</p>

<p>
  The workflow combines open-source security tools with n8n
  automation and Docker-based services to support subdomain
  enumeration, live-host identification, port discovery,
  vulnerability scanning and web content discovery.
</p>

<p>
  The project aims to reduce repetitive manual reconnaissance
  tasks while providing a structured approach to collecting
  and processing security assessment results.
</p>

<hr>

<h2>Technology Stack</h2>

<ul>
    <li>n8n</li>
    <li>Docker</li>
    <li>Subfinder</li>
    <li>HTTPX</li>
    <li>Naabu</li>
    <li>Ffuf</li>
    <li>Nuclei</li>
</ul>

<hr>

<h2>Project Goals</h2>

<ul>
    <li>Discover subdomains within authorised bug bounty program scopes</li>
    <li>Identify live hosts and web services</li>
    <li>Perform automated port discovery</li>
    <li>Detect known vulnerabilities using Nuclei</li>
    <li>Automate content discovery with FFUF</li>
    <li>Reduce manual reconnaissance effort</li>
</ul>

